description:
FILED s543m (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-24), found writing member 1's guard row (#5310).  PRE-EXISTING: base 9fc6583b the same.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl; scratch/s543m/p1/fs.pl):
    no warnings;
    { use feature "signatures"; }
    my $f = sub(r) {}; print "ok\n";
  perl: ok        PCL: PCL: statement dropped at fs.pl line 3: my $f = sub(r) {}; -- Bug. Fell through. Missing case: [funcall, Structure::Block<{}>]

WHAT IT IS (suspect, not measured): the `signatures` feature enabled INSIDE a closed block is read as still in force after it, so the anonymous sub's prototype of letters `(r)` is taken for a signature and the statement is not lowered (a counted drop).  perl scopes `use feature` to the block.  Check which reader answers "is the feature in force here" for an anonymous sub head (the vendored PPI's presumed_features or Parser's head_is_signature) and whether a named sub / a `($$)` prototype shows the same leak.  Rare (a prototype of letters is perl's "Illegal character in prototype" warning), but a statement drop.
